menu "WP News"

config WP_NEWS_TIMEZONE
    string "Local timezone (POSIX TZ)"
    default "KST-9"
    help
      POSIX TZ string for the header clock. There is no RTC on the EE04, so the
      clock comes entirely from SNTP and this is what turns UTC into what the
      panel shows.
      Examples: "KST-9" (Korea), "JST-9" (Japan), "EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0"
      (US Eastern), "CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3" (Central Europe), "UTC0".

config WP_NEWS_POLL_SECONDS
    int "News poll interval (seconds)"
    default 60
    range 30 86400
    help
      How often the device fetches the news snapshot. Polling costs nothing
      visible — the panel is only refreshed when the fetched content actually
      differs from what is on the glass — so the floor here is about not
      hammering somebody's laptop, not about e-Paper wear.

      It is not free on battery, though, and that is the number to set this by:
      a wake costs roughly 0.04 mAh, so a minute's cadence is about 58 mAh a day
      against a quarter-hour's 3.8. On USB it makes no difference at all.

      A snapshot older than twice this interval — or a quarter of an hour,
      whichever is longer — is badged "오래됨".

config WP_NEWS_FEED_URL
    string "Fallback news URL"
    default ""
    help
      Used only when no URL was entered during captive-portal setup. Leave empty
      and the board renders its built-in demo snapshot with a DEMO badge, which
      is a complete and intentional configuration — the display works with no PC
      running at all.

endmenu
